    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table, keeping each piece of logic in its natural home:\n\n1. **`Regions.java`** (the single source of truth for region logic) \u2014 added the `REGION_TIMEZONES` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneOf(region)` lookup, alongside the existing `rangeOf`/`regionOf*` methods.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getTimezone()` getter that maps the owner's existing `getLocality()` through `Regions.timezoneOf(...)`, reusing the locality derivation rather than re-deriving the region.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` property to the OwnerDto schema (right after `locality`), so the generated DTO gets the field and MapStruct auto-maps `Owner.getTimezone()` \u2192 `OwnerDto.timezone` in the response.\n\nThe acceptance test (`locality` = \"NSW\" \u2192 `timezone` = \"Australia/Sydney\") and the full suite pass.",
